title: A repository with no commit yet: the panel lists the new files, the diff and a commit view do nothing harmful, a file is staged, one change unstaged (it is untracked again), all staged and the first commit made from the app; discard before the first commit loses nothing
folders: git-no-commits
expect-file: git-no-commits/a.txt :: ^a1\na2\na3\n$
expect-file: git-no-commits/src/b.rs :: ^pub fn b\(\) -> u32 \{\n    1\n\}\n$
expect-file: git-no-commits/.git/logs/HEAD :: commit \(initial\): the first one
forbid-log: script: ignoring

wait 3000
left changes
wait 500
mark 1-panel
wait 500
diff on
wait 1200
commit 0
wait 1200
commit off
diff off
wait 800
git discard
wait 600
mark 2-discard-asked
wait 500
answer Discard
wait 1500
mark 3-after-discard
wait 500
git stage a.txt
wait 1200
part unstage a.txt 2
wait 1500
mark 4-unstaged-part
wait 500
git stage
wait 1200
git commit the first one
wait 2000
mark 5-first-commit
wait 500
quit
